<P STYLE="margin-bottom: 0cm"><B>Copyright and Intellectual Property Statement</B></P>

<p>We respect the intellectual property of others, and we ask our users to do the same.</p>

<p>At the same time, many of the web pages on our servers are electronically generated from publicly available databases (which are not associated or related to our websites in any way) in response to searches made by users on the internet, and although we do take steps to ensure that our websites do not contain any content which violates the intellectual property of others, it is not impossible that a search generated by a user may include intellectual properties, either within the results of a search or in the body of the search term.</p>

<p>Some of our web pages may contain links to other web sites which are owned and operated by third parties. These web sites are outside our control and we are not associated with them.</p>

<p>If you believe that your work has been copied or used in a way that constitutes copyright infringement, or your intellectual property rights have been otherwise violated, please provide us with the following information:</p>

<p><ol>
   <li>an electronic or physical signature of the person authorized to act on behalf of the owner of the copyright, trademark or other intellectual property interest;</li>

   <li>a description of the copyrighted work or other intellectual property that you claim has been infringed;</li>

   <li>a description of where the material that you claim is infringing is located on the site (i.e. the url of the specific page);</li>

   <li>your address, telephone number, and email address;</li>

   <li>a statement by you that you have a good faith belief that the disputed use is not authorized by the copyright or intellectual property owner, its agent, or the law;</li>

   <li>a statement by you, made under penalty of perjury, that the above information in your Notice is accurate and that you are the copyright or intellectual property owner or authorized to act on the copyright or intellectual property owner's behalf.</li>

   <li>in the case of registered trademarks, it will expedite the handling of the case if you provide details of the registration (i.e. the registration number, country of registration, etc). This is not required, but it will enable us to repsond to you and to take appropriate remedial action more quickly.</li>
</ol></p>
